  "question": {
    "text": "A wire of resistance $20 \\Omega$ is divided into 10 equal parts, resulting pairs. A combination of two parts are connected in parallel and so on. Now resulting pairs of parallel combination are connected in series. The equivalent resistance of final combination is _____ $\\Omega$.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/YS9YIvMwQjSEwiNOPV4cqQLz1eM7iCA5IaWu3M_bsTM.original.fullsize.png\"><br />Each part has resistance $=2 \\Omega$\n2 parts are connected in parallel so, $\\mathrm{R}=1 \\Omega$\nNow, there will be 5 parts each of resistance $1 \\Omega$, they are connected in series.\n$\\mathrm{R}_{\\mathrm{eq}}=5 \\mathrm{R}, \\mathrm{R}_{\\mathrm{eq}}=5 \\Omega$",
    "image": null
